  "question": {
    "text": "If $\\alpha x+\\beta y=109$ is the equation of the chord of the ellipse $\\frac{x^2}{9}+\\frac{y^2}{4}=1$, whose mid point is $\\left(\\frac{5}{2}, \\frac{1}{2}\\right)$, then $\\alpha+\\beta$ is equal to :"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "58",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "46",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "37",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "72",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"assets\\st0011_34b9257570f8.png\"><br>\n\n\n\n\nEquation of chord T $=\\mathrm{S}_1$\n$\\begin{aligned}\n& \\frac{5}{2}\\left(\\frac{x}{9}\\right)+\\frac{1}{2}\\left(\\frac{\\mathrm{y}}{4}\\right)=\\frac{25}{36}+\\frac{1}{16} \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow \\frac{5 \\mathrm{x}}{18}+\\frac{\\mathrm{y}}{8}=\\frac{100+9}{144}=\\frac{109}{144} \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow 40 \\mathrm{x}+18 \\mathrm{y}=109 \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow \\alpha=40, \\beta=18 \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow \\alpha+\\beta=58\n\\end{aligned}$"
  }
}